# Frontend (Admin + Storefront)

## API-driven UI

- Production flows must call the Express backend — no mock data as the source of truth
- Respect existing request/response contracts; map in dedicated API/mapper modules
- Never compute authoritative price/tax/shipping/coupon/inventory client-side for checkout or order write paths

## Reuse

- Inspect existing components, layouts, forms, and lib/api clients before adding new ones
- Follow established Admin/storefront patterns (nav, status badges, forms, loading UX)

## UX requirements

- Responsive Admin and storefront (desktop/tablet/mobile)
- Explicit loading, error, and empty states
- Form validation with clear field errors
- Accessible labels, focus, and keyboard-usable controls

## Next.js

This repo uses Next.js 16 with breaking changes. Before new App Router APIs, check `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` under the app you are editing. Keep `admin/AGENTS.md` and `frontend/AGENTS.md`.
